Fictional EP Tracklist

Track 1: The Mercator Line Dissolves at 0400 Hours
- Story & Context: Recorded live as the market gates swung open, this track captures the exact moment Madame Vane accidentally dropped a needle on a Chopin nocturne while a deathrock band was soundchecking on the adjacent barge. The resulting collision caused a canal-side riot among the early-morning flower vendors, cementing the genre's signature rhythm. Listeners can hear actual iron locks clicking in time with the 175-BPM snare drum. Vane shrieks the iconic hook over a weeping string quartet that suddenly detonates into fuzz-drenched punk chaos: "We erased the border just to watch the ink bleed through!"
